From: David J. Vandenburgh <david@vandenburgh.co>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm: count the msm DPU output LUTs as plane colour management

0011 keeps SDR content in the native gamut wherever planes cannot be
colour managed, so a frame looks the same whether it composites or scans
out. Its DRM answer was drm_supports_color_mgmt(), the AMD plane LUTs,
which msm never has. With 0020 a directly scanned-out SDR frame on a
DPU with DSPP LUT blocks gets the composite's gamma 2.2 shaper and 3D LUT post-blend,
and 0022 gives scanned-out HDR layers their own, so both paths carry the
same transform there and Steam's colour vibrancy (the SDR gamut wideness)
can apply to both. Count SupportsOutputLUTs() as plane colour management;
a CRTC without the DSPP LUT blocks keeps the native gamut.

The LUT rebuild skip compared only the convar. The effective choice now
also follows the backend: the output LUTs are a property of the CRTC, so
an output without them must rebuild in the native gamut.
---
diff --git a/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp b/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
index f62b5570..76ff3b93 100644
--- a/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
+++ b/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
@@ -4755,7 +4755,9 @@ namespace gamescope
 
 		virtual bool SupportsPlaneColorManagement() const override
 		{
-			return SupportsColorManagement();
+			// The msm DPU output LUTs carry the composite's gamma 2.2 shaper + 3D LUT for a
+			// frame that scans out directly, so the SDR remap reaches both paths there too.
+			return SupportsColorManagement() || SupportsOutputLUTs();
 		}
 
 		// A pair built for the previous color state is still applied for the one
diff --git a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
index db0c0ffa..0b4bf82b 100644
--- a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
@@ -667,10 +667,11 @@ update_color_mgmt()
 	struct timespec t0, t1;
 #else
 	// check if any part of our color mgmt stack is dirty
-	// The native-gamut convar feeds the LUT build, not the compared state, so a flip must
-	// get past the dirty check on its own.
-	static bool s_bLastNativeGamut = cv_color_mgmt_native_gamut_without_plane_cm;
-	const bool bNativeGamut = cv_color_mgmt_native_gamut_without_plane_cm;
+	// The native-gamut choice feeds the LUT build, not the compared state, so a change must
+	// get past the dirty check on its own: the convar, or the plane colour management it
+	// keys on (the DPU output LUTs follow the CRTC, so another output can lose them).
+	const bool bNativeGamut = cv_color_mgmt_native_gamut_without_plane_cm && !GetBackend()->SupportsPlaneColorManagement();
+	static bool s_bLastNativeGamut = bNativeGamut;
 	if ( gamescope::ColorMgmtLutsAreCurrent(
 		g_ColorMgmt.pending == g_ColorMgmt.current,
 		g_ColorMgmt.serial != 0,
